{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "האדם", :translit "ha'adam", :gloss "the man"} {:he "אדמה", :translit "adamah", :gloss "earth"} {:he "אדם", :translit "adam", :gloss "man"} {:he "אפר דם מרה", :translit "efer dam marah", :gloss "ashes, blood, bile"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Letters of האדם rearrange to אדמה: man named for the earth he was made from."} {:kind :notarikon, :word "אדם", :expansion ["אפר" "דם" "מרה"]}], :frame {:text "Genesis 2:7 records that man was formed from the dust of the earth (עפר מן האדמה). The name אדם is linked to אדמה already in that verse. The notarikon reading אדם as אפר דם מרה reflects the rabbinic tradition that the human body is composed of baser substances; the four humors are discussed in rabbinic medical contexts (e.g., Berakhot 60b, which references מרה as one of the bodily fluids).", :sources ["Genesis 2:7" "Berakhot 60b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Letters of האדם rearrange to אדמה: man named for the earth he was made from.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :notarikon, :word "אדם", :expansion ["אפר" "דם" "מרה"], :initials ["א" "ד" "מ"], :by :selah, :initials-match? true}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:03:39.145038604Z", :model "glm-5.2"}